{"t": 171.12, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Parallel-SSHI-Zener", "rationale": "The Reference FBR failed due to insufficient power (S2, S4) and overvoltage/ripple (S3). I am proposing a Parallel Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) topology. By adding an inductor L1 and a switch S1 that flips the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at its extrema, we significantly increase the energy extracted per cycle, which should fix the Vout_min and startup failures. To address the Vout_max and ripple failures in S3, I have added a Zener diode (DZ33) as a clamp on the output node and a larger storage capacitor. This combination provides higher efficiency, voltage regulation, and reduced ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Parallel-SSHI-Zener", "rationale": "The Reference FBR failed due to insufficient power (S2, S4) and overvoltage/ripple (S3). I am proposing a Parallel Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) topology. By adding an inductor L1 and a switch S1 that flips the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at its extrema, we significantly increase the energy extracted per cycle, which should fix the Vout_min and startup failures. To address the Vout_max and ripple failures in S3, I have added a Zener diode (DZ33) as a clamp on the output node and a larger storage capacitor. This combination provides higher efficiency, voltage regulation, and reduced ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 1e-05}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n